liblsl (1.17.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian/NeuroDebian packaging.
    Fills a long-standing gap: liblsl is not in Debian, Ubuntu or NeuroDebian;
    upstream ships only non-policy GitHub release .debs.
  * Build the shared library (liblsl.so.2, ABI version 2) with CMake.
  * Build offline against the system pugixml (-DLSL_FETCH_PUGIXML=OFF) instead
    of the upstream FetchContent download; bundled header-only Boost and asio.
  * Split into liblsl2 (runtime, Multi-Arch: same) and liblsl-dev (headers +
    CMake LSL::lsl imported target).

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Sat, 20 Jun 2026 10:15:00 -0700
